					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12273129#post-4326166</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12273129/adoption-poster:darius#post-4326166</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 09 Aug 2019 11:51:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>ch00bakka</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1238719</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>So it's funny and the twist is cute but there's a few things that stop me from upvoting it.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">specifically...</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">this&nbsp;stuff</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>dorm inspector</p> </blockquote> <p>i have no idea what this is. either you're looking for &quot;RA&quot; (Resident Advisor), the student who's sort of generally responsible for the safety of a door floor, or this is an actual thing at some colleges that i've never heard of.</p> <blockquote> <p>Brock Sampson</p> </blockquote> <p>naming characters directly after other characters bugs the shit out of me and anyway it's Brock Samson. as long as this is his name I can't in good conscience upvote this</p> <blockquote> <p>good conscious</p> </blockquote> <p>did you see that segue? it's &quot;good conscience&quot;. unless this is an in-universe mistake, but there's no other mistakes in that paragraph, so it just seems lazy.</p> </div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
